  "fields": {
    "title": "Title",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The title is the text, that is displayed in a browser's title bar or a page's tab, like this:",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "target": {
              "sys": {
                "id": "3zKo1w9lFuCgGIkJYGwciL",
                "type": "Link",
                "linkType": "Asset"
              }
            }
          },
          "content": [],
          "nodeType": "embedded-asset-block"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The title tag defines the document's title and is therefore important for search engines. In general, a longer, descriptive title performs better than short or generic titles regarding search engine optimization. Also, the title together with the ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6Bp9D2SYEOkA0RDwkTiEBs",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "favicon",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " is the first impression of readers looking through the search results page. The title helps people to recognize (and maybe remember) a website, without the need to open it. The title is not only visible in the browser tab, but also in the bookmark list (favorites section).",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "Thats why you can compare the the title (and the favicon) of a website to the spine of a book. Like standing in front of a bookshelf and looking for a specific book, the spine or the favicon can help you finding what you were looking for by having a recognizable design.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Possibilities",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The title element can only contain text, but you can still spice it up and use emojis or other unicode symbols.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
